  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Noddy. Type: Point-trick (Cribbage ancestor). 2-4 players. 4 cards each, no crib. Scoring: fifteens=2, pairs=2, runs=1 per card, flush=varies. Ace=1 only. Target: 31 or 61.',
    Player: 'Play Noddy, the ancestor of Cribbage. Four cards each, no crib. Score points for fifteens, pairs, runs, and flushes. First to 31 wins!',
    objective: 'Score points through card combinations (fifteens, pairs, runs, flushes) and be first to reach the target score (typically 31 or 61).',
    gameplay: '1. Four cards dealt to each player. 2. Non-dealer cuts for starter card (turn-up). 3. Players alternately play cards to the pile, pegging points for fifteens, pairs, runs during play. 4. After all cards played, hands are counted for combinations. 5. Starter card applies to both hands.',
    keyRules: [
      'Four cards dealt (no crib)',
      'Ace always counts 1 (never 11)',
      "Starter card (turn-up) counts for both players' hands",
      'Play to 31 without exceeding during pegging',
      'Similar pegging and counting to Cribbage but simpler',
    ],
